# The E2E receipt fixture is a hand-written PDF (scripts/make-receipt-fixture.ts):
# pure ASCII, so git's content heuristic reads it as text and core.autocrlf
# rewrites its line endings on checkout — which shifts every byte offset in its
# xref table and leaves an invalid PDF behind. Declaring the binary formats
# explicitly is the fix; without it the file survives hashing (the test derives
# the SHA-256 at runtime) but stops being a document any reader can open.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
